          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When a breaker finder fails, the order of checks is what saves time: transmitter lights and outlet first, then receiver battery and sensitivity, then the electronics on the circuit, then AFCI breakers and panel quirks. Most problems are solved in the first three steps.
          </p>
